  "what_this_is": "Canonical latest-pre-tip-off report designations for every 2025-26 regular-season game, counted by game date and by reporting-cadence era. Report STATUS only, which is the conversion model's input; no participation outcome is consulted and none exists in the database this was generated from. Produced by a report-only sweep against a THROWAWAY database, deliberately: the injury-report backfill needs tip-off instants, and sourcing those from ScheduleLeagueV2 would degenerate the cohort manifest's cross_source_tipoff_reconciliation into comparing one endpoint with itself. A count never becomes a manifest, so a disposable database is the right home for it.",
  "why_canonical_counts_are_a_conservative_bound": "Direct outcomes are a subset of canonical observations - rows with unresolved identity or with no participation row are excluded - so a status failing the activation floor here can never pass, while a status clearing it here is not yet proven to clear it. The bound errs toward doing more work, which is the right direction for a gate whose failure mode is wasting hours."
}
